        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Schneefernerhaus, Zugspitze, Alps, Wetterstein Mountains, Germany\n- Organizations: Environmental research station\n- Concepts: Mountain elevations, former hotels\n\nFacts:\n- The Schneefernerhaus was opened on 20 June 1931.\n- The Schneefernerhaus is a former hotel in the Alps that is now used as an environmental research station.\n- The Schneefernerhaus lies immediately below the summit of the Zugspitze at a height of 2,650 m.\n- The Zugspitze has an elevation of 2,962 m above sea level.\n- The Zugspitze is the highest peak of the Wetterstein Mountains.\n- The Zugspitze is the highest mountain in Germany.",
